---
import ToolLayout from '../../../components/ToolLayout.astro';
---
<ToolLayout
  title="Markdown Formatter & Linter – Check Markdown Privately | MarkdownMaster"
  description="Check Markdown headings, lists, whitespace, and code fences in your browser. Review safe fixes with a diff before you apply them — no upload or sign-up."
  canonical="https://markdownmaster.site/tools/markdown-linter/"
  heading="Markdown Formatter & Linter"
  intro="Check Markdown before you publish. Review safe formatting fixes and structural issues locally — nothing is uploaded."
  toolName="MarkdownMaster Markdown Formatter & Linter"
  relatedGuideHref="/blog/markdown-for-developers-readme-docs-wikis/"
  relatedGuideLabel="Read the developer Markdown guide"
>
  <style>
    .source-bar { display:flex; align-items:center; min-height:2.3rem; margin:0 0 .85rem; padding:.5rem .7rem; border:1px solid rgba(14,165,233,.38); border-radius:8px; background:rgba(14,165,233,.08); color:#bae6fd; font-size:.84rem; }
    .workspace-controls { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:.75rem; flex-wrap:wrap; margin:0 0 .85rem; }
    .workspace-controls p { margin:0; color:var(--text-muted); font-size:.82rem; }
    .control-buttons { display:flex; gap:.5rem; flex-wrap:wrap; }
    .control-buttons button, .tool-actions button, [role='tab'] { min-height:40px; border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px; padding:.55rem .8rem; background:transparent; color:var(--text); font:600 .86rem var(--font); cursor:pointer; }
    .control-buttons button:hover, .tool-actions button:hover:not(:disabled), [role='tab']:hover { border-color:var(--accent); color:var(--accent); }
    .control-buttons button:focus-visible, .tool-actions button:focus-visible, [role='tab']:focus-visible, .issue:focus-visible { outline:3px solid rgba(14,165,233,.55); outline-offset:3px; }
    .workspace-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.08fr) minmax(0,.92fr); gap:1rem; min-height:510px; }
    .input-pane, .review-pane { min-width:0; border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:10px; background:#0b1220; overflow:hidden; }
    .review-pane { display:flex; flex-direction:column; background:rgba(15,23,42,.72); }
    .pane-heading { display:flex; align-items:flex-start; justify-content:space-between; gap:.7rem; min-height:44px; padding:.75rem .9rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); color:var(--text-dim); font-size:.78rem; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.045em; text-transform:uppercase; }
    .pane-heading label { color:var(--text-dim); }
    .pane-heading output { max-width:65%; color:var(--text-muted); font-size:.72rem; font-weight:500; letter-spacing:0; line-height:1.35; text-align:right; text-transform:none; }
    #markdown-input { display:block; width:100%; min-height:465px; border:0; outline:0; resize:vertical; background:transparent; color:#dbeafe; font:.88rem/1.65 var(--font-mono); padding:1rem; tab-size:2; }
    #markdown-input:focus { box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(14,165,233,.65); }
    .review-heading { margin:0; padding:.75rem .9rem .15rem; color:var(--text); font-size:1rem; }
    [data-summary] { min-height:2.5rem; margin:0; padding:.25rem .9rem .7rem; color:var(--text-dim); font-size:.85rem; line-height:1.45; }
    [data-issues] { flex:1; min-height:150px; max-height:285px; overflow:auto; border-top:1px solid var(--border); border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); }
    .issue-group { padding:.65rem .75rem; }
    .issue-group + .issue-group { border-top:1px solid rgba(51,65,85,.72); }
    .issue-group h3 { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; margin:0 0 .45rem; color:var(--text-dim); font-size:.72rem; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.05em; text-transform:uppercase; }
    .issue-group h3 span { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; min-width:1.35rem; min-height:1.35rem; border-radius:999px; background:rgba(148,163,184,.12); font-size:.7rem; }
    .issues-empty { margin:0; padding:1rem .9rem; color:#86efac; font-size:.86rem; }
    .issue { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.25rem minmax(0,1fr) auto; gap:.55rem; align-items:start; padding:.6rem .5rem; border-radius:7px; cursor:pointer; }
    .issue:hover { background:rgba(148,163,184,.08); }
    .issue-control { padding-top:.1rem; }
    .issue-control input { width:1rem; height:1rem; accent-color:var(--accent); cursor:pointer; }
    .issue-review-dot { display:block; width:.7rem; height:.7rem; margin:.22rem 0 0 .15rem; border:2px solid #fbbf24; border-radius:50%; }
    .issue-title { margin:0; color:var(--text); font-size:.8rem; font-weight:700; line-height:1.4; }
    .issue-title code { color:var(--accent-hover); font:600 .72rem var(--font-mono); }
    .issue-copy > p:not(.issue-title) { margin:.18rem 0 0; color:var(--text-muted); font-size:.77rem; line-height:1.45; }
    .issue-copy .issue-suggestion { color:#fcd34d; }
    .issue-line { padding-top:.1rem; color:var(--text-muted); font:500 .7rem var(--font-mono); white-space:nowrap; }
    .result-tabs { display:flex; gap:.3rem; padding:.65rem .75rem 0; }
    [role='tab'] { min-height:32px; padding:.38rem .6rem; border-radius:6px; color:var(--text-dim); font-size:.76rem; }
    [role='tab'][aria-selected='true'] { border-color:rgba(14,165,233,.65); background:rgba(14,165,233,.1); color:var(--accent-hover); }
    [data-result-panel] { min-height:145px; max-height:220px; overflow:auto; margin:.55rem .75rem .75rem; border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px; background:#070d18; color:#dbeafe; font:.76rem/1.55 var(--font-mono); tab-size:2; }
    .result-panel--formatted { padding:.75rem; white-space:pre; }
    .diff-line { display:grid; grid-template-columns:2.3rem 2.3rem 1rem minmax(0,1fr); min-width:max-content; padding:0 .55rem; white-space:pre; }
    .diff-number { color:#64748b; text-align:right; user-select:none; }
    .diff-marker { padding-left:.4rem; color:#94a3b8; }
    .diff-line--added { background:rgba(34,197,94,.12); }
    .diff-line--added .diff-marker { color:#86efac; }
    .diff-line--removed { background:rgba(248,113,113,.12); }
    .diff-line--removed .diff-marker { color:#fca5a5; }
    .tool-actions { display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; gap:.65rem; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:.9rem; }
    .tool-actions button.primary { border-color:transparent; background:var(--accent); color:#082f49; }
    .tool-actions button.secondary { background:transparent; }
    .tool-actions button:disabled { cursor:not-allowed; opacity:.5; }
    [data-tool-status] { display:block; min-height:1.45rem; margin:.7rem 0 0; color:var(--text-muted); font-size:.84rem; }
    [data-tool-status][data-kind='success'] { color:#86efac; }
    [data-tool-status][data-kind='error'] { color:#fca5a5; }
    .linter-details { margin:2.2rem 0 .25rem; padding-top:1.7rem; border-top:1px solid var(--border); }
    .linter-details h2 { margin:0 0 .7rem; color:var(--text); font-size:1.15rem; }
    .linter-details p { margin:.6rem 0; color:var(--text-dim); font-size:.9rem; line-height:1.7; }
    .checks-table { width:100%; margin:1rem 0; border-collapse:collapse; font-size:.82rem; }
    .checks-table th, .checks-table td { padding:.65rem; border:1px solid var(--border); color:var(--text-dim); text-align:left; vertical-align:top; line-height:1.55; }
    .checks-table th { color:var(--text); background:rgba(14,165,233,.07); }
    .workflow-links { display:flex; gap:.65rem; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:1rem; }
    .workflow-links a { display:inline-flex; padding:.58rem .72rem; border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px; color:var(--text); font-size:.84rem; text-decoration:none; }
    .workflow-links a:hover { border-color:var(--accent); color:var(--accent); }
    @media (max-width:760px) {
      .workspace-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; min-height:auto; }
      #markdown-input { min-height:310px; }
      [data-issues] { max-height:none; }
      [data-result-panel] { max-height:220px; }
      .tool-actions > button { flex:1 1 calc(50% - .4rem); }
      .pane-heading { align-items:flex-start; }
    }
    @media (max-width:460px) {
      .workspace-controls { align-items:stretch; }
      .control-buttons { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); }
      .control-buttons button { padding-inline:.45rem; font-size:.78rem; }
      .tool-actions > button { flex-basis:100%; }
      .checks-table { display:block; overflow:auto; }
    }
  </style>

  <div class="source-bar" data-source-bar hidden></div>
  <div class="workspace-controls">
    <p>Safe fixes are never applied until you review them.</p>
    <div class="control-buttons" aria-label="Markdown document actions">
      <button type="button" data-action="load-sample">Load example</button>
      <button type="button" data-action="import">Import .md</button>
      <button type="button" data-action="clear">Clear</button>
      <input id="markdown-file-input" type="file" accept=".md,.markdown,.mdx,text/markdown,text/plain" hidden />
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="formatter-workspace" aria-label="Markdown formatting workspace">
    <div class="workspace-grid">
      <section class="input-pane" aria-labelledby="markdown-input-label">
        <div class="pane-heading">
          <label id="markdown-input-label" for="markdown-input">Markdown input</label>
          <output data-document-stats>0 characters · 0 lines</output>
        </div>
        <textarea id="markdown-input" maxlength="524288" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="formatter-status" placeholder="# Project title\n\nPaste Markdown here to check it locally..."></textarea>
      </section>

      <section class="review-pane" aria-labelledby="review-heading">
        <h2 class="review-heading" id="review-heading">Review</h2>
        <p data-summary role="status" aria-live="polite">Checking Markdown locally…</p>
        <div data-issues></div>
        <div class="result-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Formatting result">
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-tab="diff">Diff</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="formatted">Formatted Markdown</button>
        </div>
        <div data-result-panel tabindex="0" aria-label="Formatting result"></div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <p id="formatter-status" data-tool-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div class="tool-actions">
      <button class="secondary" type="button" data-action="undo" disabled>Undo</button>
      <button class="secondary" type="button" data-action="open-editor">Open in editor</button>
      <button class="secondary" type="button" data-action="copy">Copy formatted Markdown</button>
      <button class="primary" type="button" data-action="apply" disabled>Apply selected fixes</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="linter-details" aria-labelledby="formatter-details-heading">
    <h2 id="formatter-details-heading">Format Markdown without losing control</h2>
    <p>MarkdownMaster checks common spacing, list, heading, and code-fence issues in your browser. When a change is safe and predictable, you can review it in a line-by-line diff before applying it. When a decision depends on your document’s meaning, the tool flags it for review and leaves the choice to you.</p>

    <h2>What this Markdown linter checks</h2>
    <p>Use the standard check before you publish a README, API reference, technical note, or release update. It can normalize heading and list spacing, remove accidental whitespace, replace tabs outside code blocks, reduce extra blank lines, and add a final newline. It also highlights structural issues that need an author’s judgment.</p>
    <table class="checks-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Safe fixes you can review</th><th>Checks that need your decision</th><th>What this tool does not do</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody><tr><td>Heading and list spacing, extra blank lines, accidental trailing spaces, and final newlines.</td><td>Heading hierarchy, duplicate headings, code language labels, image alt text, and possible link syntax problems.</td><td>It does not rewrite prose, test remote links, upload files, or guarantee every Markdown renderer behaves the same way.</td></tr></tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Use it before you publish documentation</h2>
    <p>Start with a practical structure, then check formatting before you publish. Use a template for a GitHub README, API documentation, or release notes, and return to the Markdown editor when you need a live preview.</p>
    <div class="workflow-links">
      <a href="/templates/github-readme-template/">Open the GitHub README template</a>
      <a href="/templates/api-parameter-documentation-template/">Start with the API documentation template</a>
      <a href="/templates/release-notes-template/">Use the release notes template</a>
    </div>

    <h2>Private by design</h2>
    <p>Your Markdown is processed in this browser. MarkdownMaster does not upload your document, file name, or formatting results to a server. Optional anonymous analytics are disabled unless you allow them and never include your Markdown text.</p>
  </section>

  <script>
    import '../../../scripts/markdownLint/controller';
  </script>
</ToolLayout>
